# Copilot-Aligned Execution Rule

- Follow mandatory read order before code/API/schema/service/UI edits:
  1) `.github/personal-game-dev-skill.md`
  2) `DOCUMENTATION_GUIDE.md`
  3) `API_REFERENCE.md` (for API-related work)
  4) `.github/copilot-instructions.md`
- Reuse existing architecture and services before creating new abstractions.
- Make the smallest safe change that satisfies the request.
- Keep UX and interaction patterns consistent with existing pages/components.
- If behavior/contracts/workflow change, update relevant docs in the same task:
  - `API_REFERENCE.md`
  - `DOCUMENTATION_GUIDE.md`
  - `.github/copilot-instructions.md`
  - `TACTICAL_GUIDE.md` (when tactical/wording impact exists)
- Prefer end-to-end completion: implement, verify, and report.
- Validation expectation: run appropriate checks (`lint`, `build`, or targeted tests) when changes are substantive.
